                    {
                        "sense_id": "7dcd173f-28ba-3fec-a62a-36f951a78e60",
                        "entry_id": "ca2676e5-983d-31b4-bbc0-798f06fd048f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "fern (plant of division Pteridophyta)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "510eb0ff-2fad-4888-abfb-7496dd79eabd",
                                "sense_id": "7dcd173f-28ba-3fec-a62a-36f951a78e60",
                                "text": "liść paproci",
                                "translation": "frond (literally, “leaf of a fern”)",
                                "english": "frond (literally, “leaf of a fern”)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cbfb4a69-ff57-48be-8183-2d6cb328470c",
                                "sense_id": "7dcd173f-28ba-3fec-a62a-36f951a78e60",
                                "text": "Była w Słowiaństwie wówczas osławiona — ¶ Zober nazwana — czarodziejska góra, ¶ Skalny szczyt miała — na buków ramiona ¶ Włożony — w chmurach wisiała, jak chmura. ¶ Na niej pustelnia stała postawiona, ¶ Ubrana w osty — i w paproci pióra; ¶ I trzej mięszkali, mówią, pustelnicy ¶ Pod strażą — orła, gadziny[,] i lwicy.",
                                "translation": "There was in the Slavness an ill-famed — ¶ Zober named — magical mountain, ¶ It had a rocky peak — into the arms of the beeches ¶ Inserted — hanged in the clouds, like a cloud. ¶ On it stood a hermitage, ¶ dressed in thistles — and in the feathers of a fern; ¶ And three hermits, they say, lived here ¶ Under the guard of — an eagle, a creeping animal[,] and a lioness.",
                                "english": "There was in the Slavness an ill-famed — ¶ Zober named — magical mountain, ¶ It had a rocky peak — into the arms of the beeches ¶ Inserted — hanged in the clouds, like a cloud. ¶ On it stood a hermitage, ¶ dressed in thistles — and in the feathers of a fern; ¶ And three hermits, they say, lived here ¶ Under the guard of — an eagle, a creeping animal[,] and a lioness."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd49c5a7-b247-4812-b17b-ad0cd5443a14",
                                "sense_id": "7dcd173f-28ba-3fec-a62a-36f951a78e60",
                                "text": "Wieje gorący samum ¶ miechów ¶ nad paleniskiem [kuźni]: ¶ kwitną w upalnym oddechu ¶ tropikalne paprocie iskier."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
